From bf8cd31e5f3c5293e28194db118479e1428859a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:55:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): remote_links_and_origin_rows takes stale_ok for
 display routes [daveey]

hermes-mods bfe75689 made user-steps /session-cards read terminal history through
remote_links_and_origin_rows(), which is always strict: it computes
_links_fingerprint() and waits on the global _links_lock while any projection runs.
On hermes-hub (serve PID 460982) that route had 11 of 31 requests over 2 s, max
7.1 s, with stacks parked on the `with _links_lock:` line, while the stale-only
/api/session-kanban-tasks stayed under 1.5 s. test_web_links_stale
[user-steps-ledger] and [user-steps-unreadable-replica] fail against that plugin.

remote_links_and_origin_rows(stale_ok=False) now forwards stale_ok to
_links_entry. The default stays strict: chat-closeout needs read-your-writes. A
warm stale entry already carries the origin rows (entry[4]) and returns before any
fingerprint or lock work; a cold scope still projects synchronously.

run_tests.sh forwards HERMES_TEST_USER_STEPS_API through its env -i, so
test_web_links_stale can be pointed at a candidate plugin worktree (it was a
silent no-op before: the cases always loaded ~/code/hermes-mods).

Proof:
- New tests in test_kanban_links_stale_scopes.py: stale_ok=True returns the warm
  (cards, rows) entry while the fingerprint is held; the default still waits.
  Mutants killed: forwarding False again fails the stale test; defaulting
  stale_ok=True fails the strict test.
- With the patched plugin (HERMES_TEST_USER_STEPS_API): test_web_links_stale 8
  passed, 0 skipped; with the current hermes-mods plugin, 2 failed as on the hub.
- 15-file suite tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_{links,replica,busy,remote_inventory,
  chat_links,session_activity}*.py tests/hermes_cli/test_web_links_stale.py plus
  tests/scripts/test_run_tests_shell.py: 199 passed, 0 failed.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_session_activity.py         | 10 ++-
 scripts/run_tests.sh                          |  5 +-
 .../test_kanban_links_stale_scopes.py         | 65 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hermes_cli/kanban_session_activity.py b/hermes_cli/kanban_session_activity.py
index 911fc2f87e..e62fad78e0 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/kanban_session_activity.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/kanban_session_activity.py
@@ -893,11 +893,15 @@ def _links_fingerprint() -> tuple:
     return tuple(signature)
 
 
-def remote_links_and_origin_rows() -> tuple[list[dict[str, Any]], list[dict[str, Any]]]:
+def remote_links_and_origin_rows(stale_ok: bool = False) -> tuple[list[dict[str, Any]], list[dict[str, Any]]]:
     """[daveey] ``(_remote_links(), origin rows)`` from one cached projection: the origin rows are the ledger
     ``project()`` rows behind the cards, released rows included (the cards omit those). Plugins that need released
-    rows (chat-closeout) take them here instead of projecting the ledger again on every pass."""
-    return _links_entry(False, with_rows=True)
+    rows (chat-closeout) take them here instead of projecting the ledger again on every pass.
+
+    The default stays strict (read-your-writes) for closeout-style callers. Display routes that are documented as
+    stale-only (user-steps session-cards) pass ``stale_ok=True``: a warm entry, rows included, returns before any
+    fingerprint or ``_links_lock`` work and refreshes in the background; a cold scope still projects synchronously."""
+    return _links_entry(stale_ok, with_rows=True)
 
 
 def _remote_links(stale_ok: bool = False) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
